# Editor-only include paths.
#
# The real build compiles against build/lib — the PATCHED copy that
# scripts/apply_patches.sh produces — so that directory must come FIRST here.
#
# Pointing the editor at the pristine src/dsp/lib instead does NOT work: our
# patch ADDS a defaulted parameter to KeyframeRecorder::Init, and an added
# parameter is very much visible to name resolution. Against the pristine
# header every two-argument Init call reads as "too many arguments".
#
# build/ is gitignored, so on a fresh checkout clangd will report the vendored
# headers as missing until you run `scripts/apply_patches.sh` (or any
# `make -C tests/host test`, which runs it as a prerequisite). That is the
# right trade: transiently-missing headers are a clearer signal than
# confidently-wrong arity errors.
#
# This affects the editor only. Nothing reads it at compile time.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -std=c++17
    - -I../../build/lib
    - -I../../src/dsp
    - -Ibuild/lib
    - -Isrc/dsp
    - -Wno-unused-parameter
